// The milestone-1 FREESTANDING skeleton -- the first Omega image booted under
// real UEFI firmware (QEMU/OVMF, 2026-07-03: "Image Return Status = Success",
// and returning 5 printed "Warning Stale Data" -- the return value flows
// through RAX to the firmware).
//
// `subsystem efi_application` makes the target FREESTANDING: it trusts no host
// boundary packages (absence = denial), so the backend builds against an empty
// host ABI plan -- zero bindings, zero import thunks, and the PE emitter's
// empty-import-table path produces a clean import-free PE32+ subsystem-10
// image. With no data fields the image also has zero absolute fixups, so an
// arbitrary-base load (OVMF) is trivially sound. The entry's literal terminal
// lands in EAX and `ret` returns it to the firmware as the EFI_STATUS.
data Main { }

machine Main::main(&mut self) -> i32 {
    transition { _ -> (0) }
}
